<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  One entitlement, and it buys one thing: a parent's own devices pair without
  a screen.

  iCloud key-value store is per APPLE ID, not per family. My iPhone and the
  family iPad, yes, automatically. Two parents are two Apple IDs and nothing
  Apple exposes joins them — there is no family identifier available to a
  third-party app, deliberately, and ownershipType == .familyShared says an
  entitlement arrived through a family without carrying a key to pair on. That
  is why the QR exists and why it is not going away.

  NOT iCloud Documents and NOT CloudKit. This carries three short strings; a
  container would be a second backing store beside the API we already run.

  Every failure here is silence by design: no iCloud account, iCloud Drive off,
  a device never online — NSUbiquitousKeyValueStore keeps working as a local
  plist and never syncs. Nothing to surface, nothing for a parent to fix, and
  the QR still works. Invariant 11's philosophy, applied to pairing.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.developer.ubiquity-kvstore-identifier</key>
	<string>$(TeamIdentifierPrefix)$(CFBundleIdentifier)</string>
</dict>
</plist>
